title: The Saxon Election
subtitle: Saxony elects a new Landtag.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 11
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
var r = RG.election('saxony', {
    base: {spd: 40, kpd: 10, dnvp: 19, dvp: 19, ddp: 8},
    size: 96,
    kpdShare: 10.5,
    bonus: (Q.e22_reunification == 1 ? 1 : 0) + (Q.e22_inflation_line == 1 ? 0.5 : 0)
});
Q.e22_sax_spd = r.seats.spd || 0;
Q.e22_sax_right = (r.seats.dnvp || 0) + (r.seats.dvp || 0) + (r.seats.ddp || 0);
Q.e22_sax_majority = Q.landtag_saxony_left_majority;
Q.e22_sax_stood = Q.election_kpd_share > 0 ? 1 : 0;
Q.e22_sax_gain = Q.election_kpd_seats - 10;
if (Q.e22_sax_stood) {
    Q.district_saxony_members *= 1 + Math.max(0, Q.election_kpd_share - 6) / 100;
}
if (Q.e22_sax_majority) {
    RG.news('Saxony: the workers\' parties win a majority in the Landtag', 3);
} else {
    RG.news('Saxony: no majority for the workers\' parties', 3);
}
!}

= The Saxon Election

On 5 November Saxony elects a new Landtag. [? if e22_sax_stood = 1 : The party wins [+ election_kpd_share_display +] per cent of the vote and [+ election_kpd_seats +] seats. ?][? if e22_sax_stood = 0 : The party stands no candidates, on principle. ?] The SPD wins [+ e22_sax_spd +], and the bourgeois parties [+ e22_sax_right +] between them. [? if e22_sax_majority = 1 : Together the two workers' parties hold [+ election_left_seats +] of the ninety-six seats. In Saxony, at least, the bourgeois parties can be outvoted. ?][? if e22_sax_majority = 0 : The workers' parties hold [+ election_left_seats +] of the ninety-six seats, short of a majority. The Saxon SPD can govern only with the Democrats, or with our votes and theirs. ?]

[? if e22_sax_gain >= 3 : It is the party's best result anywhere in Germany, and the Chemnitz district secretaries are photographed for the first time in their lives. ?][? if e22_sax_gain <= -3 : It is a disappointment: the hungry winter has not come to our lists. ?]

The Saxon SPD is the most left-wing in Germany. Its members sing the *Internationale* at their meetings and many of them would rather govern with us than with the Democrats. Its leaders want our votes for a Social Democratic government. They ask what our price is.

[? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg writes that a workers' majority in one Land is a school, not a revolution, and that the party must not be afraid to sit its exams. ?]

- @tolerate: Support an SPD government, on conditions: control committees, a workers' militia, a purge of the monarchist officials.
- @ministers: Demand seats in the government: a real workers' government.
- @refuse: No support for Social Democratic ministers.

@tolerate
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Right's road. Saxony becomes our showcase, and our responsibility.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids supporting a Social Democratic government.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e22_saxon_toleration = 1;
RG.ecci('radek', 3);
RG.district('saxony', {militancy: 2});
Q.spd_relation += 6;
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.district_saxony_loyalty += 6;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 5;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The SPD accepts most of our conditions on paper. A Social Democratic minority government takes office in Dresden with our votes, and the control committees get a legal footing.

@ministers
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Only possible if the Saxon SPD trusts us. Bold, and Berlin will be alarmed.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2 and spd_relation >= 35 and e22_sax_majority = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The SPD will not take communist ministers without a majority, or the line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e22_saxon_toleration = 3;
Q.saxony_government = 1;
RG.ledger('Communist ministers entered the Saxon government, a year early.', 'e22_sax_ministers');
RG.news('Two communists join the Saxon cabinet', 2);
RG.ecci('radek', 6);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -3);
Q.spd_relation += 4;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.repression += 4;
Q.district_saxony_loyalty += 8;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 8;
Q.lean_unionist += 3;
!}

After a month of talks, two communists take seats in the Saxon cabinet. It is the first time our party has held ministries anywhere in Germany. The Reichswehr commander in Dresden asks Berlin for instructions.

@refuse
subtitle: The Left's answer. The SPD governs with the Democrats, and blames us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_saxon_toleration = 2;
RG.ecci('radek', -4);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 2);
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
Q.district_saxony_loyalty -= 5;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 8;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Our deputies vote against every candidate for Minister-President. The Saxon SPD forms a minority government with the Democrats' tolerance, and its members ask our members what they are for.
